WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.042
A method is a function that belongs to a class.

00:00:03.042 --> 00:00:07.457
When a function is written inside a class, we usually call it a method.

00:00:07.457 --> 00:00:12.282
A method can use the data stored inside an object.

00:00:12.282 --> 00:00:16.427
The word self is how a method refers to the current object.

00:00:16.427 --> 00:00:22.902
For example, if we have self.price and self.quantity, the method is using the price and quantity stored in

00:00:22.902 --> 00:00:24.332
the object that called the method.

00:00:24.332 --> 00:00:28.622
This may feel strange at first, but the idea is practical.

00:00:28.622 --> 00:00:33.892
If we create several objects from the same class, each object has its own data.

00:00:33.892 --> 00:00:39.767
The method needs a way to know which object's data to use.

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:41.532
That is the role of self.

00:00:41.532 --> 00:00:45.962
In the Sale example, the total method multiplies self.price by self.quantity.

00:00:45.962 --> 00:00:49.652
The method does not need us to pass price and quantity again,

00:00:49.652 --> 00:00:53.242
because those values are already stored inside the object.

00:00:53.242 --> 00:00:58.877
So the main idea is: attributes store data, methods define actions,

00:00:58.877 --> 00:01:02.160
and self connects a method to the specific object using it.
